course: dictionary
lesson: 16000
title: Saying goodbye: the valediction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A valediction is a formal word for a goodbye. It can be the act of saying goodbye, or the words you use to say it. Writers use it when they want to sound polite and serious, like in a letter or a speech.
explain: Look for the clues. «Her valediction was a long wave from the platform.» Here, the wave is the goodbye, so valediction means the act of saying goodbye. Ask yourself: what is happening? Are people leaving, ending a letter or giving a speech? That tells you which kind of goodbye it is.
explain: In a letter, the valediction is the sign-off at the end. «Yours sincerely» and «Best wishes» are valedictions because they close the letter politely. In everyday talk, you would just say goodbye or sign off, but in formal writing, valediction is the right word.
fact: Valediction means the act of saying goodbye, or the words used to say goodbye.
fact: A valediction can be a goodbye speech or a goodbye poem.
fact: The closing words of a letter, such as «Yours sincerely» or «Best wishes», are a valediction.
fact: In the USA and Canada, a valedictorian is the top student who gives the goodbye speech at graduation.
fact: Valediction is a formal word. In everyday talk, people say goodbye or sign-off instead.
exercise: «Her valediction was a long wave from the platform.» What does valediction mean here? | A type of train ticket | A loud argument | A birthday present | *The act of saying goodbye
exercise: In a letter, where do you find the valediction? | In the title | *At the end, as a sign-off | At the top, with the address | In the middle of the paragraph
exercise: Find and copy one word that means saying goodbye: «Her valediction at the end of the year made us all smile.» | made | year | *valediction | smile
test: «The old poem ended with a sad valediction.» In this poem, what is a valediction? | *A farewell | A question about the weather | A list of names | A song about rain
test: Which of these is a valediction? | A list of school subjects | A question you ask in class | *A closing like «Best wishes» at the end of a letter | A title like «Mr Smith» at the top of a page
exam: In the USA, the valedictorian gives the valediction at graduation. What does valediction mean here? | *A goodbye speech | A test paper | A kind of school lunch | A type of school bag
